{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1407587-clarification-on-some-cantrips","id":1407587,"title":"Clarification on some Cantrips","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-11T15:14:25-07:00","id":1407587,"title":"Clarification on some Cantrips","content":"Hi, I've been having doubt about the effects of a few Cantrips and was wondering if some of you had answers.<br /> <br /> -Veiled Eyes (Chicanery): If a Changling is the target of this Cantrip, would the Cantrip be Chimerical or Wyrd?<br /> <br /> -Elder-Form (Primal): Are those enchanted with wood unable to move, or merely impossible to move against their will?<br /> <br /> -Enkindle (Summer): Would the Cantrip force people to act on the inflamed emotion? If not, what would it actually do, mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T21:17:36-07:00","id":1407860,"title":"","content":"if the target can see the dreaming (chimera, changeling, inanimae, enchanted human, kinain, etc) the art can be cast as chimerical if said option is possible. However it can also be advantageous to cast it as wyrd in some situations even if chimerical is a option.<br /> <br /> If you turn into a tree you're unable to move. Unless you turn into a ghille dhu appearance (so, a tree with legs and arms) maybe? But if you turn into a usual tree, you're no moving anywhere, trees don't walk.<br /> <br /> Enkindle don't force people to act on the inflamed emotion, but it's not unusual to happen. It's usually decided by roleplay I suppose. Unless wea re talking NPC, then some storytellers might do a willpower roll to see if the target acts on the emotion. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T14:33:08-07:00","id":1408791,"title":"","content":"Regarding Veiled Eyes, cast as chimerical it will stop people who can perceive the dreaming from noticing that the person is a changeling, cast as wyrd nobody will notice that someone is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}